/-
# Son's sextic relation (B) — GENERATED by scripts/septic/make_son_B.py (+ gen_son.py)

`a(b²c³ + c²d³ + d²b³) = a³bcd + 2(bcd)²` with `a, b, c, d = T 0, T 1, T 2, T 3`.

**Proof (6-dimensional isometry).** `M` below is an integer matrix with `MᵀM = 49·I`, so `g = M/7` is a rational
orthogonal map of `ℝ⁶`. Its reduction mod 7 has rank 2; the row space `U` is a totally isotropic plane of `F₇⁶`
and `g` maps the lattice `L_U = {k ∈ ℤ⁶ : k mod 7 ∈ U}` isometrically onto `L_U'` (`U'` = column space).
Hence `Σ_{k∈L_U} q^{|k|²} = Σ_{k∈L_U'} q^{|k|²}`; splitting each side by `k mod 7` (49 cosets) gives
`P_U(a,b,c,d) = P_U'(a,b,c,d)`, and `P_U − P_U' = -12·(B)`. Pure counting, as in `Quaternion.lean`.

`M` = [[-3, 1, -3, -1, -5, 2], [-1, 3, -2, -5, 3, -1], [2, 5, -1, 3, 1, 3], [1, 3, 5, -2, -3, -1], [-5, 2, 1, 3, 1, -3], [3, 1, -3, 1, -2, -5]]
-/
